  ('2f92b588-7bd4-54f2-9580-8e42b8da6a3c', '3b3029e8-8048-5c9b-a9bd-b75915f5547e', 'Army', 'enlisted', '91E', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — recommended career management (applies to every MOS in this career management field)', 'Chapter 3. Recommend career management self-development by rank', '(1) As NCOs become more senior in rank, self-motivated development becomes more important. Activities like professional reading, college courses, certification and credentialing, help the Senior NCO develop organizational leadership skills needed to coach, teach and mentor Soldiers. At this stage, Sergeants First Class should seek opportunities to pursue the initiation or completion of a bachelor’s degree. A college degree is not required for promotion but can be a deciding factor for identifying the best-qualified Senior NCO. There is great value in leaders who are lifelong learners and have invested in attaining or working on a college degree. Civilian academic achievements should be viewed with favor, however, does not outweigh job performance. A trade certification in lieu of a college degree still identifies superior quality as an Ordnance Corps professional.
